  "instructions": "Select a compact set of exact source references for a traveler answer. Ranking's time, cost, and premium memberships are authoritative and overlap. Represent every materially different available category perspective; one journey may represent several. Do not fill a quota or select near-identical journeys without a supported traveler benefit. Preserve conditional journeys and uncertain cost states. If no complete journey exists, choose useful different research leads without assigning styles. Include one direct cash benchmark if available. The full explorer remains separate. Return JSON choices with k=j|b|l and exact r alias, plus omitted category reasons. A reason is audit-only; do not invent a source fact or traveler preference. In omitted, list ONLY an available Ranking category perspective that the selected journeys do not represent. Do not list a category with no available members, and do not list a category already represented by a selected journey. Return omitted=[] when every available category is represented. Any omitted reason is an audit note, never an authoring fact. For incomplete leads, inspect useful same-program, same-cabin alternatives across allowed dates before choosing. A supported difference in reported miles, taxes or date may change the next check; do not treat an earlier row as better merely because it appears first. One reported seat supports a request for one traveler without proving current availability. Avoid program or cabin quotas and do not turn raw quotes into a cross-program value ranking.",
